# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
#
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo reads it
# when minting a DOI for a release. Keep `version` and `date-released` in step
# with track2data/_version.py and the tag -- tests/test_version_consistency.py
# checks the first of those.
#
# TODO(maintainer): add `orcid:` below, and the release DOI under
# `identifiers:` once the Zenodo-GitHub integration is switched on. See
# docs/dev/RELEASING.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Track2Data: analysis-ready behavioural datasets from idtracker.ai output"
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite both this entry
  and idtracker.ai (Romero-Ferrero et al. 2019), the tracker whose output it
  consumes.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bellio
    given-names: Martina
    email: m.bellio2199@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mbel-tech/Track2Data"
url: "https://github.com/mbel-tech/Track2Data"
abstract: >-
  Track2Data converts idtracker.ai session folders into analysis-ready
  behavioural datasets. It computes 45 individual-, group- and zone-level
  metrics, each carrying a citation to the work defining it, alongside
  tracking-quality diagnostics that report how much of every value rests on
  measured rather than reconstructed positions. Exports ship a machine-
  readable codebook of units and DOIs, per-session recording metadata, and a
  manifest recording every parameter and an input checksum, so a result can
  be traced back to the bytes that produced it.
keywords:
  - animal behaviour
  - behavioural phenotyping
  - collective behaviour
  - idtracker.ai
  - trajectory analysis
  - zebrafish
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-10-09"

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      idtracker.ai: tracking all individuals in small or large collectives of
      unmarked animals
    authors:
      - family-names: Romero-Ferrero
        given-names: Francisco
      - family-names: Bergomi
        given-names: Mattia G.
      - family-names: Hinz
        given-names: Robert C.
      - family-names: Heras
        given-names: Francisco J. H.
      - family-names: de Polavieja
        given-names: Gonzalo G.
    journal: Nature Methods
    volume: 16
    start: 179
    end: 182
    year: 2019
    doi: 10.1038/s41592-018-0295-5
    notes: >-
      The upstream tracker. Track2Data reads its session folders and does not
      perform tracking itself.
